  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SECURING GRAUER S GORILLA POPULATION STRONGHOLDS IN THE KAHUZI-BIEGA NATIONAL PARK AND SURROUNDING OKU COMMUNITY FORESTS, DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS 3-YEAR COOPERATIVE AGREEMENT IS TO SECURE THE SINGLE LARGEST POPULATION STRONGHOLD OF GRAUER S GORILLA IN EASTERN DRC. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: 1) STRENGTHENING THE PROTECTION OF THE KAHUZI-BIEGA NATIONAL PARK (KBNP) THROUGH IMPROVED LAW ENFORCEMENT CAPACITY AND EFFECTIVENESS 2) EXTENDING FORMAL PROTECTION TO 60% OF THE REMAINING POPULATION OF GRAUER S GORILLAS, AND 60% OF THEIR HABITAT, THROUGH THE CREATION OF A NEW FORMAL PROTECTED AREA THE OKU COMMUNITY RESERVE - BORDERING THE KBNP 3) BUILDING CONSERVATION PARTNERSHIPS WITH LOCAL COMMUNITIES AND REINFORCING EXISTING SUSTAINABLE LIVELIHOOD INITIATIVES TO MITIGATE LOCAL DRIVERS OF HUNTING PRESSURE ON GRAUER S GORILLAS 4) IMPLEMENTING A FIELD MONITORING AND RESEARCH PROGRAM THAT MEASURES PROJECT IMPACT AND GUIDES PROJECT CONSERVATION INTERVENTIONS AND 5) WORKING WITHIN EXISTING MONITORING STRUCTURE TO PROMOTE AND FACILITATE A STAKEHOLDER COLLABORATION SUB-WORKING GROUP FOCUSING ON MINING AND OTHER THREATS TO THE SPECIES.</narrative>
  </description>
